#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:9
msgid "⚠ Mode check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:11
msgid ""
"This skill describes the **legacy** workflow where the agent hand- writes"
" the agent half of `NEXT.md`. If the project has run `hero next migrate-"
"to-projection` (config: `next.projected: true` in `.hero/hero.json`), "
"NEXT.md is now graph-projected — anything you write to it gets wiped on "
"the next Stop hook. Use the [next-handoff-emit](next-handoff-emit.md) "
"skill instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:18
msgid ""
"To check: `hero next` — if the file's `updated:` frontmatter timestamp "
"moves on every Stop hook, projection is on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:21
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:23
msgid ""
"Define the shape of NEXT.md — the single living artifact that lets a "
"fresh session (or one resuming after compaction) pick up exactly where "
"the last one left off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:27
msgid "NEXT.md is split in two halves:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md
msgid "Half"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md
msgid "Who writes it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md
msgid "When"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"**Agent half** — Last user ask, Just finished, Next, Blocked on, Tried "
"and failed, Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md
msgid "The agent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"When the intent shifts, something fails, an approach gets rejected, or "
"you're about to switch tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md
msgid "**Machine half** — Branch, recent commits, working tree, hot files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md
msgid "`hero next checkpoint` (run by a host-tool Stop hook)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md
msgid "Every turn, automatically"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:34
msgid ""
"The agent never has to write the machine half. The harness keeps it fresh"
" on every turn — no agent discipline required. The agent's only job is "
"the agent half."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:38
msgid "`.hero/next/<user>.local.md` is machine-state-only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:40
msgid ""
"The gitignored per-machine state file `.hero/next/<user>.local.md` is "
"**rebuilt wholesale on every checkpoint** — it contains the marker- "
"bounded machine block and nothing else. **Never hand-edit it. Never write"
" scratch into it. Anything outside the marker block is wiped on the next "
"Stop hook** (the first time a wipe happens, the prior hand-content is "
"backed up once to `<user>.local.md.bak.<timestamp>` so an accidental loss"
" is recoverable, then discarded on subsequent runs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:49
msgid ""
"If you want a preserved per-machine briefing the agent doesn't touch, "
"write to a separately-named file such as `.hero/notes/<user>.md` — no "
"Hero tool reads or rewrites that path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:53
msgid "Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:55
msgid "Run `hero next path` to get the file path you should write to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:57
msgid "**Solo mode** (default): writes `.hero/NEXT.md` — one shared briefing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:58
msgid ""
"**Team mode** (`next.mode: \"team\"` in `hero.json`): writes "
"`.hero/next/<user>.md` — your personal briefing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:61
msgid ""
"In team mode, also update your one-liner in the shared `.hero/NEXT.md` "
"roster so teammates see what you're working on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:64
msgid "When to use me"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:66
msgid ""
"**At session start:** read your NEXT file (via `hero next path`) before "
"doing anything else and surface it to the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:68
msgid ""
"**During the session:** the agent overwrites the agent half when the "
"triggers below fire. The Stop hook keeps the machine half fresh; you do "
"not need to run it manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:72
msgid "Format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:74
msgid ""
"The agent owns everything *above* the `<!-- BEGIN HERO MACHINE STATE -->`"
" marker. Always overwrite the entire agent half. Never append. Aim for "
"15-40 lines in the agent half; hard cap 60."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:78
msgid ""
"---\n"
"updated: 2026-04-22T15:30:00Z\n"
"session: <host-tool>/<model>\n"
"branch: <git-branch>\n"
"---\n"
"\n"
"## Last user ask\n"
"<1-3 lines, the user's own words, from their most recent meaningful\n"
"turn. The single most expensive thing for a fresh session to recover.>\n"
"\n"
"## Just finished\n"
"<What shipped this turn. Commit hash + message if one was made.\n"
"Note any uncommitted state.>\n"
"\n"
"## Next\n"
"<The concrete next step. One short paragraph plus a runnable pointer.>\n"
"\n"
"→ <runnable pointer: a slash command, spec path, or shell command>\n"
"\n"
"## Blocked on (omit if clear)\n"
"<Test failures, build errors, things you got stuck on. Include the\n"
"actual error message or file/line.>\n"
"\n"
"## Tried and failed (omit if N/A)\n"
"<Approaches that didn't work, so the next session doesn't suggest them\n"
"again. One line per rejected idea.>\n"
"\n"
"## Context to carry forward (omit if nothing meaningful)\n"
"<Non-obvious decisions, user preferences, open questions. Compaction-\n"
"survival kit, not a transcript.>\n"
"\n"
"## Proposed next ask\n"
"<One paste-ready sentence the user could say to resume productive\n"
"work. Phrased as the user would phrase it, not as instructions to\n"
"the agent. The \"when in doubt, just look it up\" answer for the next\n"
"session opener.>\n"
"\n"
"<!-- BEGIN HERO MACHINE STATE -->\n"
"[…auto-written, do not touch…]\n"
"<!-- END HERO MACHINE STATE -->\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:121
msgid "Section guidance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:123
msgid ""
"**Last user ask** — quote the user's wording. Don't paraphrase. A fresh "
"session reading this should immediately know what the user wants. If the "
"last meaningful ask was 3 turns ago and the recent turns have been "
"conversational, quote that earlier ask."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:127
msgid ""
"**Just finished** — one bullet per concrete thing. Skip if you only read "
"code or had a discussion. The machine half already lists commits and "
"dirty files; only mention what's *interesting* (e.g. \"shipped X, but "
"uncommitted because Y\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:131
msgid ""
"**Next** — concrete next step plus the `→ <pointer>` line. The pointer "
"must be runnable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:133
msgid "**Blocked on** — only if actually stuck. Copy the real error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:134
msgid "**Tried and failed** — gold. One line per rejected approach."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:135
msgid ""
"**Context to carry forward** — only what isn't derivable from `git log`, "
"the spec corpus, or the codebase. Skip the heading entirely if empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:137
msgid ""
"**Proposed next ask** — the user's perspective, paste-ready. One "
"sentence, no command names, no file paths unless the user would naturally"
" name them. The bar: a fresh session that pastes this verbatim should "
"kick off productive work without needing to read the rest of the file. "
"Think *\"continue with the e2e suite for discovery, same shape as "
"onboarding\"*, not *\"run scripts/e2e/ discovery.sh\"*. Skip if the next "
"move genuinely depends on the user's state (e.g. they're about to make a "
"strategic decision only they can make)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:147
msgid "When to update the agent half"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:149
msgid ""
"The Stop hook handles the machine half every turn — the auto-half also "
"auto-summarizes commits + AC status flips since the prior checkpoint, so "
"most \"what just happened\" is captured for free."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:153
msgid "The single rule for the agent half:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:155
msgid ""
"**Read the file as it stands. Could a fresh session pick up correctly "
"from this right now? If no, update it. If yes, leave it.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:158
msgid ""
"Apply this rule before handing back to the user, before invoking another "
"agent or skill, and any time you're about to claim a piece of work is "
"done. The bar is *correctness of the handoff*, not \"did anything "
"change.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:162
msgid "Concrete failure modes that flip the answer to **no**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:164
msgid ""
"The \"Last user ask\" no longer reflects what the user actually wants "
"(intent shifted, or the user gave new instructions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:166
msgid ""
"\"Just finished\" omits a meaningful commit or spec status change a fresh"
" session would need to know about."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:168
msgid "\"Next\" points at work that's already done, or doesn't exist anymore."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:169
msgid ""
"\"Blocked on\" is silent about a real blocker, or claims one that's been "
"resolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:171
msgid ""
"\"Tried and failed\" is missing an approach you just rejected — the next "
"session would re-suggest it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:174
msgid ""
"If none of those apply, leave the file alone. Conversational turns "
"(*\"explain this\", \"what would you suggest\"*) almost never flip the "
"rule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:177
msgid ""
"Don't write a fresh agent half just because commits landed — the machine "
"half lists those automatically. Update the agent half when the "
"**narrative** would mislead a fresh session, not when the activity log "
"grew."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:182
msgid "Quality bar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:184
msgid ""
"A good NEXT.md is one a fresh session can read and immediately be "
"productive without asking \"what were we doing?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:187
msgid "The new session should know:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:189
msgid "**What the user actually wants** — last user ask, in their words"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:190
msgid "**What just shipped** — agent half + machine commits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:191
msgid "**What's blocked** — actual error messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:192
msgid "**What to do next** — a runnable pointer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:193
msgid "**What NOT to try** — approaches already rejected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:195
msgid ""
"If you can't picture a fresh session being productive after reading it, "
"add detail. If it's becoming a transcript, cut detail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:198
msgid ""
"**Hard cap on agent half: 60 lines. Target: 15-40.** If you need more, "
"move detail to `.hero/knowledge/notes/` and link it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:201
msgid "Shared file (team mode only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:203
msgid "In team mode, `.hero/NEXT.md` is the team's shared file with two roles:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:205
msgid "1. Roster — always update your line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:207
msgid ""
"## Working on\n"
"\n"
"- **chet-bellows**: delivering challenge-diagnosis spec (Apr 23 14:30)\n"
"- **alice**: fixing auth timeout bug #142 (Apr 23 11:15)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:214
msgid "2. Updates — only when something affects others"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:216
msgid ""
"## Updates\n"
"\n"
"### Apr 23 — chet-bellows\n"
"Shipped drift detection — `hero drift` is live, affects all spec "
"workflows.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:223
msgid "Most turns don't warrant a team update. If unsure, skip it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:225
msgid "What not to do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:227
msgid "Don't append history — overwrite the agent half every time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:228
msgid ""
"Don't touch the `<!-- BEGIN HERO MACHINE STATE -->` … `<!-- END … -->` "
"block. The Stop hook owns it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:230
msgid ""
"Don't write a fresh agent half after every prompt. Only when something in"
" the trigger list above fired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:232
msgid ""
"Don't include large diffs, code snippets, or full spec contents — point "
"at the artifact instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:234
msgid ""
"Don't paraphrase what's already in the spec corpus or the codebase. The "
"handoff is the *delta* not visible elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-md/SKILL.md:236
msgid ""
"**Don't hand-edit `.hero/next/<user>.local.md`.** It is rebuilt every "
"checkpoint and any content you write outside the marker block will be "
"discarded. Use `.hero/notes/<user>.md` (or any path not under "
"`.hero/next/`) for preserved per-machine notes."
msgstr ""

